Notes
- Implemented: All 10 functional requirements are present in code (smart contract + backend + frontend integration).
- Automated tests: Backend unit tests executed via Maven; smart-contract tests exist but Hardhat run was blocked by compiler/compat issues (see below).
- Test results: Backend test run produced 13 tests (9 passed, 1 failure, 3 errors). See `backend/target/surefire-reports` for details.

Key pointers
- Smart contract: `hardhat/contracts/LandVerification.sol` and tests at `hardhat/test/LandVerification.multisig.test.js`
- Backend tests: `backend/src/test/java` (e.g. `TransferServiceTest.java`, `LandParcelServiceTest.java`)
- Frontend integration: `frontend/public/js/api.js` and pages under `frontend/public/pages`

How to reproduce locally
1) Run backend unit tests (Maven):

```powershell
mvn -f "backend/pom.xml" test
```

2) Run smart-contract tests (Hardhat). Ensure Node.js >=18 and dependencies installed:

```bash
cd hardhat
npm install
npm test -- test/LandVerification.multisig.test.js
```

If Hardhat reports compiler errors related to OpenZeppelin, ensure `hardhat.config.js` solidity version matches OpenZeppelin contracts (this repo set to 0.8.24).

Exporting the diagram for Word
- Option A (quick): Install the `Markdown Preview Enhanced` or `Mermaid Preview` VS Code extension, open this `.mmd` file and export PNG/SVG from the preview.
- Option B (CLI): Install `@mermaid-js/mermaid-cli` and run:

```bash
npx mmdc -i docs/requirements-coverage.mmd -o docs/requirements-coverage.png
```

Troubleshooting
- Backend test failures: see `backend/target/surefire-reports` for stack traces; run `mvn -f backend/pom.xml test -DskipITs -e` for full logs.
- Hardhat failures: run `npx hardhat compile --show-stack-traces` inside `hardhat/` to see compilation errors; you may need to align Solidity pragma versions or update OpenZeppelin dependency versions.
